1
00:00:05,183 --> 00:00:08,621
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:09,096 --> 00:00:10,580
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

3
00:00:11,827 --> 00:00:14,276
So now, covered Baiyah Tul Aqabal Al-Uolaa(بيعة العقبه الأولى)

4
00:00:14,451 --> 00:00:16,691
The first Pledge of Allegiance of Al-Aqabah(العقبه),

5
00:00:16,737 --> 00:00:21,207
which were, the terms of it would called the Pledge of Allegiance of the women.

6
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:27,170
Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير), has done a outstanding work in spreading the message

7
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:33,221
 and by the time the next Hajj(حَجْ) season arrived,

8
00:00:33,709 --> 00:00:35,769
the narrator of the Hadith(حديث) says

9
00:00:35,809 --> 00:00:41,063
there was no house in Madina that didn't have a Muslim in it.

10
00:00:42,172 --> 00:00:43,865
Look at the effort of Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير).

11
00:00:44,947 --> 00:00:50,943
So now the appointment to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ, in pilgrimage was approaching.

12
00:00:51,625 --> 00:01:01,640
So, over 70 of the Muslims went with the pilgrims of their people.

13
00:01:03,042 --> 00:01:06,926
So, the delegation that came out of Madina included Muslims and non Muslims.

14
00:01:07,718 --> 00:01:10,840
And the Muslims had a secret appointment with Muhammadﷺ,

15
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:16,003
but they went out with the group that was leaving from Madina.

16
00:01:16,423 --> 00:01:20,825
So there are over 70 men who are Muslim and two women.

17
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:28,047
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), he narrates the following story.

18
00:01:28,253 --> 00:01:29,142
He says;

19
00:01:29,354 --> 00:01:34,043
We were among the pilgrims of our people, some were Muslim and some were non Muslim.

20
00:01:35,104 --> 00:01:41,064
And our leader and elder was Al-Baraa Bin Ma'rur(ألبرآء بن معرور)

21
00:01:41,826 --> 00:01:44,408
He was the leader among the Muslims.

22
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:48,632
Ka'ab Ibn Malikرضي الله عنه said;

23
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:52,803
that Al-Baraa Bin Ma'rur(ألبرآء بن معرور) came to us, in a group of the Muslims.

24
00:01:53,137 --> 00:01:59,356
And he said: I have an idea and I want to get your opinion,

25
00:02:01,042 --> 00:02:07,364
I don't feel comfortable turning my back towards this building in prayer.

26
00:02:08,896 --> 00:02:10,666
He was referring to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

27
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:14,061
What was the Qibla(قبله) of the Muslims at the time?

28
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:17,188
Praying to Al-Aksaa(اَلْاَقْصَى) Jerusalem.

29
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:24,790
So, the people who are in Madina, they are facing Jerusalem, while their backs are towards Makkah.

30
00:02:25,473 --> 00:02:29,544
So, Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور) is saying, I don't feel comfortable doing that.

31
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:36,770
And I wanted to seek your advice on whether I should pray towards Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

32
00:02:38,288 --> 00:02:40,670
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said, we responded by saying,

33
00:02:40,824 --> 00:02:45,881
Rasool Allah ﷺ is praying towards Jerusalem and we don't want to contradict him.

34
00:02:47,431 --> 00:02:50,489
Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور) said: I am gonna pray towards Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

35
00:02:52,614 --> 00:02:55,543
And from that day on, he started pray towards Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

36
00:02:57,043 --> 00:03:00,165
Now the delegation made it to Makkah,

37
00:03:00,859 --> 00:03:06,299
Al-Baraa Bin Maroor رضي الله عنه, he said to Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), he said;

38
00:03:06,339 --> 00:03:12,000
My nephew let's go off to the Messenger of Allah and asked him about what I've been doing on this journey,

39
00:03:12,436 --> 00:03:16,431
the disapproval I have seen in you has somewhat disturbed me.

40
00:03:17,008 --> 00:03:20,529
Let's go to Rasool Allah ﷺ, if what I did was right a wrong?

41
00:03:22,357 --> 00:03:26,383
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: We asked the man from Makkah, where is Rasool Allah ﷺ.

42
00:03:26,423 --> 00:03:28,367
So, the man said: Do you know him?

43
00:03:28,746 --> 00:03:29,940
Have you seen him before?

44
00:03:30,114 --> 00:03:32,694
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: No, we don't know him.

45
00:03:33,478 --> 00:03:34,979
The man responded by saying;

46
00:03:35,146 --> 00:03:37,794
Do you know Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب), his uncle.

47
00:03:38,326 --> 00:03:39,437
 They said: Yes,

48
00:03:39,958 --> 00:03:42,810
we used to see him, in Madina on business trips.

49
00:03:43,096 --> 00:03:46,761
Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) used to frequent Madina, doing business, so they knew him.

50
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:49,656
The man said:

51
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:57,148
Muhammadﷺ is the man sitting next to Al-Abbas(العباس) in the mosque, you will find him there.

52
00:03:57,809 --> 00:04:00,791
So, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: I went with my uncle Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور).

53
00:04:00,830 --> 00:04:06,081
We went into the Mosque, and we found Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب), and we came and greeted them.

54
00:04:07,229 --> 00:04:14,632
Muhammadﷺ said: O, Uncle, Abul Fazl(أبوالفضل), Do you know who these two men are?

55
00:04:15,007 --> 00:04:17,143
The elder son of Al-Abbas(العباس), his name is Al-Fazl(الفضل).

56
00:04:17,405 --> 00:04:24,346
And it was a tradition of the Arabs to give a name to the Father, the father of so and so, the eldest son.

57
00:04:24,963 --> 00:04:29,480
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Abul Fazl(ابوالفضل), Do you know, these two men?

58
00:04:29,991 --> 00:04:31,451
Al-Abbas(العباس) said: Yes.

59
00:04:31,784 --> 00:04:37,435
This is Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(البراء بن معرور), the leader of his people, and this is Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

60
00:04:39,045 --> 00:04:40,658
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said:

61
00:04:41,332 --> 00:04:49,144
I swear by Allah, I will never forget the next statement that Rasool Allah ﷺ made,

62
00:04:50,635 --> 00:04:55,173
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Do you mean, the poet.

63
00:04:56,209 --> 00:04:58,346
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) was a poet.

64
00:04:59,537 --> 00:05:03,941
So, when Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) introduced Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) to Muhammadﷺ

65
00:05:03,981 --> 00:05:05,560
and said, this is Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

66
00:05:05,791 --> 00:05:08,907
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Is he the poet?

67
00:05:09,755 --> 00:05:15,219
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says, I can never forget that statement in my whole life.

68
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:18,154
Why was it such a big deal to Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).?

69
00:05:19,162 --> 00:05:22,519
Because it shows that Rasool Allah ﷺ has heard of him.

70
00:05:23,226 --> 00:05:25,952
And Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) was so proud and happy

71
00:05:26,341 --> 00:05:33,361
that Rasool Allah ﷺ, his leader, the man who, he meets him for the first time and has been waiting for this moment to meet him,

72
00:05:33,633 --> 00:05:37,798
has heard of him, he might have even heard some of his works.

73
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:44,016
So, he was so proud and happy that Rasool Allah ﷺ has already heard of him.

74
00:05:44,637 --> 00:05:45,663
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

75
00:05:45,703 --> 00:05:46,518
ألشاعر؟

76
00:05:46,703 --> 00:05:47,983
Is he, the poet?

77
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,384
Al-Abbas said: Yes.

78
00:05:51,892 --> 00:05:53,265
Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور) said;

79
00:05:53,305 --> 00:06:02,169
O Messenger of Allah, I have come on this journey having been given guidance to Islam by Allah,

80
00:06:03,037 --> 00:06:06,748
I had the idea of not facing my back to this building.

81
00:06:06,938 --> 00:06:08,605
So, I prayed towards it,

82
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:11,930
my friends opposed me in this, causing me concern.

83
00:06:12,152 --> 00:06:13,232
What do you think?

84
00:06:14,031 --> 00:06:18,638
Muhammadﷺ said: You already had a Qibla(قبله), a direction for prayer,

85
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:20,750
and you should have kept it.

86
00:06:21,361 --> 00:06:26,628
You should have remained praying to the Qibla(قبله), that you know.

87
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:30,243
Since then, Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور) changed the direction.

88
00:06:30,449 --> 00:06:32,541
Now with Rasool Allah ﷺ at that time,

89
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:34,646
Rasool Allah ﷺ because he was in Makkah.

90
00:06:34,702 --> 00:06:37,433
He wasn't turning his back towards Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

91
00:06:37,695 --> 00:06:40,418
He was facing Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) but in the direction of Jerusalem.

92
00:06:40,646 --> 00:06:43,567
But the people of Madina, Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور) didn't like that

93
00:06:43,607 --> 00:06:45,673
 and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) when Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة),

94
00:06:45,888 --> 00:06:47,858
Rasool Allah ﷺ was feeling the same feeling.

95
00:06:51,125 --> 00:06:52,664
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said;

96
00:06:52,744 --> 00:06:54,696
We then left to the pilgrimage

97
00:06:55,046 --> 00:06:58,974
having made an agreement to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه),

98
00:06:59,014 --> 00:07:00,488
in the middle of the Tashreeq(تشريق) period,

99
00:07:00,543 --> 00:07:04,095
so they made an appointment to meet at a specific time.

100
00:07:04,710 --> 00:07:06,218
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says;

101
00:07:06,670 --> 00:07:10,911
We kept this as a secret, none of our people knew about it

102
00:07:11,006 --> 00:07:19,125
all of the non Muslims in our group, knew nothing about our meeting with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

103
00:07:19,982 --> 00:07:21,109
it was secret.

104
00:07:23,019 --> 00:07:26,247
Except Abu Jabir(ابوجابر), Abdullah Bin Haraam(عبدالله بن حرام),

105
00:07:26,813 --> 00:07:30,413
he was one of our leaders and seniors, we went up to him and we told him;

106
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:34,483
Abu Jabir(ابوجابر), you are one of our noble leaders,

107
00:07:34,713 --> 00:07:37,515
and we would like you to give up your practices,

108
00:07:37,692 --> 00:07:41,473
otherwise one day you would end up as fuel for hellfire.

109
00:07:42,589 --> 00:07:44,669
Abu Jabir(ابوجابر) did accept Islam.

110
00:07:44,812 --> 00:07:47,376
So, they told him about the private meeting,

111
00:07:47,612 --> 00:07:49,624
and he was one of the people who attended with them.

112
00:07:50,953 --> 00:07:55,904
In fact, he became one of the leaders that were appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ within this group.

113
00:07:58,827 --> 00:08:03,175
It was the time for the appointment, it was late at night.

114
00:08:05,086 --> 00:08:11,419
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: We were going towards Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه) in ones or two's.

115
00:08:12,142 --> 00:08:14,221
They didn't want to attract the attention of the people,

116
00:08:14,284 --> 00:08:19,197
if you have a group of 70 going to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ, it would turn the attention of others.

117
00:08:19,395 --> 00:08:24,621
So, they were going in ones and twos, until they all gathered in Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه).

118
00:08:25,113 --> 00:08:29,129
And they were all there, and then Rasool Allah ﷺ showed up.

119
00:08:31,033 --> 00:08:37,002
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the only Muslim from Makkah to show up at that meeting,

120
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:39,604
and he had one person with him

121
00:08:39,953 --> 00:08:43,975
and that was the only non Muslim to attend the meeting,

122
00:08:44,233 --> 00:08:45,573
and who was that person?

123
00:08:45,954 --> 00:08:49,700
Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب), the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

124
00:08:51,676 --> 00:08:55,213
And Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) was the first person to speak.

125
00:08:55,871 --> 00:08:56,713
He said;

126
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:02,296
Muhammad(محمد) holds with us a position of which you are aware.

127
00:09:03,325 --> 00:09:06,613
We protect him from our people, who think about him as we do.

128
00:09:07,375 --> 00:09:10,762
He's respected among his people and safe in his own town.

129
00:09:11,588 --> 00:09:14,050
But he is determined to join up with you.

130
00:09:14,834 --> 00:09:19,711
If you think you will keep trust with him, in the invitation you have given to him,

131
00:09:20,091 --> 00:09:25,447
and will protect him from his opponents, then it's up to you to accept your responsibilities.

132
00:09:26,132 --> 00:09:30,893
But if you think he might deliver him over, and abandon him, after he has joined you,

133
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:33,306
then leave him right now.

134
00:09:33,817 --> 00:09:38,496
He does have respect and protection among his own people and in his town.

135
00:09:39,642 --> 00:09:43,103
Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب), wanted to make sure

136
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:46,839
that this is a commitment from the side of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار),

137
00:09:47,072 --> 00:09:52,537
Al-Abbas(العباس) is saying that we are going to take care of Muhammadﷺ, we are protecting him.

138
00:09:52,849 --> 00:09:55,065
However, he is insisting on leaving us.

139
00:09:55,295 --> 00:09:58,549
Now are you going to protect him when he leaves to you or not?

140
00:09:59,987 --> 00:10:02,288
How come Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) was there?

141
00:10:02,313 --> 00:10:04,982
I mean, why was he present even though he was a non Muslim?

142
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:06,922
What is the reason he was there.?

143
00:10:06,962 --> 00:10:10,407
Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) was the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

144
00:10:10,951 --> 00:10:12,604
and even though he was a non Muslim,

145
00:10:12,793 --> 00:10:16,936
but he was one of the senior members of the clan of Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم).

146
00:10:18,036 --> 00:10:21,840
And even though he was a non Muslim, but he was taking special interest

147
00:10:21,913 --> 00:10:25,275
in following and monitoring the activities of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

148
00:10:25,849 --> 00:10:29,766
and he was one of the people, who were offering Rasool Allah ﷺ protection in Makkah,

149
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,726
after Abu Talib(ابوطالب) passed away.

150
00:10:32,393 --> 00:10:37,007
And he wanted to make sure that his nephew will be safe when he leaves Makkah.

151
00:10:39,031 --> 00:10:43,542
And that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ allowed him and included him, in this meeting,

152
00:10:43,791 --> 00:10:49,730
because even though he was a non Muslim, but this is again, an issue that relates to the tribe of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم).

153
00:10:50,010 --> 00:10:55,983
Muhammadﷺ remains as a member of this clan, and his clan have interest in his safety and security.

154
00:10:56,573 --> 00:11:02,282
So, Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) attended as a representative of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم), to make sure

155
00:11:02,602 --> 00:11:04,538
that their son is well protected.

156
00:11:05,602 --> 00:11:07,930
Now, you might say, well,

157
00:11:08,684 --> 00:11:13,746
 if Al-Abbas(العباس) was offering protection, how come it's different than the time of Abu Talib(ابو طالب)?

158
00:11:13,897 --> 00:11:19,746
Well, the difference is that Abu Talib(ابو طالب) had respect and power and authority over his people

159
00:11:19,913 --> 00:11:21,633
that none of his brothers had.

160
00:11:22,317 --> 00:11:26,721
So, the ability of Al-bbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) to defend Muhammadﷺ

161
00:11:26,761 --> 00:11:29,403
was obviously less than the ability of Abu Talib(ابوطالب)

162
00:11:29,646 --> 00:11:31,612
because of the seniority of Abu Talib(ابوطالب),

163
00:11:31,787 --> 00:11:32,998
Al-Abbas(العباس) was young.

164
00:11:33,764 --> 00:11:39,838
Nevertheless, they still managed to protect him for that period and they viewed it as responsibility on them.

165
00:11:40,962 --> 00:11:43,939
When Al-Abbas(العباس) finished his statement.

166
00:11:44,336 --> 00:11:49,399
Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) said: We have heard, what you have to say,

167
00:11:49,772 --> 00:11:54,098
Now, O Messenger of Allah, ask us what you want?

168
00:11:55,064 --> 00:11:58,693
Go ahead and speak to us about what you want from us

169
00:11:59,115 --> 00:12:02,683
and take for yourself and for your Lord, whatever you want.

170
00:12:03,954 --> 00:12:06,215
Rasool Allah ﷺ stood up and said;

171
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:12,792
 I ask you to pledge that you will defend me, as you do, your women and children.

172
00:12:13,245 --> 00:12:20,681
So now, this is an upgrade, a step higher than the earlier agreement in Baiyah Tul Aqabal Al-Uolaa(بيعة العقبه الأولى),

173
00:12:21,173 --> 00:12:23,198
 over there it is for becoming Muslim,

174
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:25,413
so they pledge allegiance on becoming Muslim.

175
00:12:25,706 --> 00:12:28,863
But now there's an additional term that was added to the contract,

176
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:35,686
and that is offering Muhammadﷺ with protection, and it's a defensive protection.

177
00:12:36,767 --> 00:12:46,960
He also told them, in a different narration, you must pledge to hear and obey at times of both action and inaction,

178
00:12:47,455 --> 00:12:53,383
to give whether times are hard or easy, and to advocate goodness and prohibit evil,

179
00:12:53,839 --> 00:12:58,168
you must speak out for Allah and not feel any blame for supporting Allah.

180
00:12:58,755 --> 00:13:01,584
You must help and defend me, if I come to you.

181
00:13:01,677 --> 00:13:06,357
In the same way you helped and defend yourselves, your wives and your children.

182
00:13:07,529 --> 00:13:11,057
You notice here the clarity, in the message of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

183
00:13:12,088 --> 00:13:16,732
I'm not coming to you, just for you to protect me, but I'm to be your leader.

184
00:13:17,261 --> 00:13:19,465
You listen to me, and you obey me.

185
00:13:20,354 --> 00:13:23,264
And then he said, and you fear no one, but Allah,

186
00:13:24,351 --> 00:13:27,497
I cannot make this move, if you have any fear in your hearts.

187
00:13:28,386 --> 00:13:32,005
You have to be willing to commit yourselves for this mission.

188
00:13:32,781 --> 00:13:40,868
Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور), he stood up and wanted to give Rasool Allah ﷺ Baiyah(بيعة)

189
00:13:41,024 --> 00:13:41,968
and he said;

190
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:50,800
O messenger of Allah, I swear it, we are warriors from father to son over many generations.

191
00:13:51,317 --> 00:13:54,876
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I wanted to protect me like you protect your women and children,

192
00:13:55,254 --> 00:13:56,448
Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور) said:

193
00:13:56,488 --> 00:14:01,222
O Messenger of Allah, we are warriors, we have inherited this, from generation to generation.

194
00:14:01,395 --> 00:14:04,058
And this is another thing Allah prepared Al-Aos wal Khazraj(الاوس والخزرج) with,

195
00:14:04,317 --> 00:14:09,018
that they were fighters, they were strong, and they had this reputation in Arabia.

196
00:14:11,404 --> 00:14:14,381
And while Al-Baraa Bin Maroor(إلبراء بن معرور) was speaking

197
00:14:15,016 --> 00:14:20,611
Abul Haitham(أبو الهيثم), stood up, and he interrupted, and he said,

198
00:14:21,055 --> 00:14:26,602
 O Messenger of Allah, we have certain ties to others, referring to the Jews,

199
00:14:27,297 --> 00:14:31,628
and if we break these, we are concerned that if God gives you victory,

200
00:14:31,822 --> 00:14:34,536
you might return to your people and abandon us.

201
00:14:35,335 --> 00:14:38,230
Abul Haitham(أبولهيثم), is saying that this commitment means

202
00:14:38,529 --> 00:14:43,523
that we will have to, we might get into conflict with people whom we have agreements with.

203
00:14:43,981 --> 00:14:48,517
So now, if in case you win, are you going to stay with us, or you going to leave us,

204
00:14:48,755 --> 00:14:54,179
 see we are willing to enter into this agreement for our whole life.

205
00:14:54,719 --> 00:14:57,809
 But are you going to stay with us or are you going to leave us.?

206
00:14:57,897 --> 00:15:00,537
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded after smiling.

207
00:15:00,679 --> 00:15:01,540
He said;

208
00:15:02,118 --> 00:15:05,495
"If your blood be sought, our blood shall be sought

209
00:15:05,897 --> 00:15:08,225
and your destruction is mine as well.

210
00:15:08,439 --> 00:15:11,181
I am of you and you are of me,

211
00:15:11,304 --> 00:15:15,141
I will battle those, who battle you and make peace with those,

212
00:15:15,329 --> 00:15:16,862
with whom you make peace."

213
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:20,029
And Rasool Allah ﷺ kept to his agreement.

214
00:15:20,425 --> 00:15:24,515
When Makkah was opened, the hometown of Rasool Allah ﷺ

215
00:15:24,846 --> 00:15:28,645
he left it and he went back with the people of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) to Madina,

216
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:30,994
And he remained there until he died.

217
00:15:31,556 --> 00:15:36,613
Rasool Allah ﷺ, stayed with the people of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), until the last moment.

218
00:15:38,405 --> 00:15:42,742
In another narration, there is another interruption,

219
00:15:44,062 --> 00:15:49,356
when the Ansaar(أنْصَار) started extending their hands to pledge allegiance to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

220
00:15:49,736 --> 00:15:55,497
As'ad Bin Zurarah(اسعدبن زرارة), the early Muslim among them, stood up and interrupted and said;

221
00:15:57,029 --> 00:16:01,053
Slowly now, he's telling his people take it easy, slow down

222
00:16:02,319 --> 00:16:06,664
We only hurried here because we know that he is the Messenger of Allah,

223
00:16:07,721 --> 00:16:13,315
bringing him out now, however, would be provocation to all the Arabs

224
00:16:13,686 --> 00:16:15,885
and would cause you to lose your elite

225
00:16:16,139 --> 00:16:19,385
and would box you in, with swords raised against you.

226
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:26,070
If you are able to withstand that, then adopt him, and it will be up to Allah to reward you.

227
00:16:26,618 --> 00:16:29,475
But if you are people who have great fear for yourselves,

228
00:16:29,658 --> 00:16:32,281
then leave him and make that fact plain,

229
00:16:32,607 --> 00:16:36,017
that coarse would be more forgivable in Allah's sight.

230
00:16:36,255 --> 00:16:40,834
He said: Do you realize what agreement we're entering in,

231
00:16:41,276 --> 00:16:47,242
If we take Rasool Allah ﷺ with us, that means that we are going against the whole world

232
00:16:47,697 --> 00:16:50,605
and will be boxed in, with swords surrounding us,

233
00:16:50,866 --> 00:16:54,970
we might lose our elites, we might spend our money,

234
00:16:55,272 --> 00:16:56,589
we might be killed.

235
00:16:56,739 --> 00:16:58,847
Now we either stand up and commit.

236
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:03,425
Otherwise, if you have any fear, in your hearts pull out now, when it's not too late.

237
00:17:04,941 --> 00:17:07,667
They pushed As'ad Bin Zararah(أسعد بن زراره) away and said;

238
00:17:07,707 --> 00:17:09,381
We will give Pledge of Allegiance.

239
00:17:09,421 --> 00:17:10,733
They said, keep away from us.

240
00:17:10,918 --> 00:17:14,335
We won't renegade on this pledge, we will never deny it.

241
00:17:14,943 --> 00:17:18,549
Allah-Ho-Akbar(الله اكبر) look at the commitment of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) and the courage that they had.

242
00:17:18,738 --> 00:17:23,067
Now, when Rasool Allah ﷺ asked them, to protect him,

243
00:17:23,701 --> 00:17:27,229
they said; What will we get in exchange.

244
00:17:27,796 --> 00:17:31,716
We are going to offer you protection even if we lose our lives and our wealth.

245
00:17:31,981 --> 00:17:34,970
What are you going to give us, this is not a one sided agreement.

246
00:17:35,259 --> 00:17:38,573
We are offering you help, what will you give us in exchange.?

247
00:17:38,613 --> 00:17:40,249
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say;

248
00:17:41,128 --> 00:17:43,313
He responded by telling them one word,

249
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:44,811
Al-Jannah(ألجنة),

250
00:17:45,107 --> 00:17:47,448
Paradise, nothing else.

251
00:17:47,824 --> 00:17:49,141
I'm not gonna give you kingdom.

252
00:17:49,301 --> 00:17:50,936
I'm not promising you wealth.

253
00:17:51,332 --> 00:17:56,571
I'm not going to give you a few cabinet seats or ministries in my government.

254
00:17:57,023 --> 00:17:59,250
 I'm not going to promise you a succession after me.

255
00:17:59,964 --> 00:18:01,892
All what I can promise you is Jannah(ألجنة).

256
00:18:02,197 --> 00:18:03,560
And what was their response,

257
00:18:04,129 --> 00:18:04,535
They said;

258
00:18:04,575 --> 00:18:07,410
 رَبِح الْبَيْعْ لَا نَقِيْلُ وَلَا نَسْتَقِيْلْ

259
00:18:07,593 --> 00:18:11,561
This is such a profitable deal, we will never give up.

260
00:18:12,639 --> 00:18:14,123
They said: what is better than Jannah(ألجنة).

261
00:18:17,310 --> 00:18:20,683
Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر) compare this with Bayhara Bin Faraas(بيحره بن فراس).

262
00:18:21,361 --> 00:18:23,944
He said: I'm going to take this young man and eat the Arabs with him.

263
00:18:24,221 --> 00:18:25,848
And then he told Rasool Allah ﷺ;

264
00:18:26,092 --> 00:18:28,947
If Allah gives you victory. Will you then transfer power to us.?

265
00:18:28,987 --> 00:18:29,817
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

266
00:18:29,850 --> 00:18:31,006
No, it's up to Allah.

267
00:18:31,181 --> 00:18:33,244
He said: We don't want to have anything with you.

268
00:18:33,534 --> 00:18:39,616
Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) said, That is the best deal, Jannah(جنة).

269
00:18:41,459 --> 00:18:48,283
Somehow the news reached to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), you know it's not easy to conceal a meeting of 70 plus people,

270
00:18:49,553 --> 00:18:52,121
in the crowd of Al-Hajj(حَجْ).

271
00:18:52,922 --> 00:18:58,107
 In one narration it states that it was Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), who announced it to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

272
00:18:58,669 --> 00:19:00,774
But regardless of how it happened.

273
00:19:01,012 --> 00:19:03,035
The news reached to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

274
00:19:04,292 --> 00:19:08,568
they investigated the matter further and they found out, it led them to the right direction,

275
00:19:08,608 --> 00:19:10,054
it led them to Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

276
00:19:11,293 --> 00:19:16,383
So, next day early in the morning, a group of leaders from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

277
00:19:16,652 --> 00:19:20,869
went and visited the campgrounds of Al-Aos wal Khazraj(الاوس والخزرج).

278
00:19:21,544 --> 00:19:29,074
They went to them and said: We have heard that you have met with Muhammadﷺ,

279
00:19:29,527 --> 00:19:33,368
 and that you have offered to take him with you and give him protection.

280
00:19:34,039 --> 00:19:42,790
Now, listen people of Yasrib(يثرب), you are the last people on the face of the earth, whom we want to have a fight with.

281
00:19:43,468 --> 00:19:47,327
Because Quraish(قريش) knew that Al-Aos wal Khazraj(الاوس والخزرج) were not an easy opponent.

282
00:19:47,843 --> 00:19:49,133
These are fighters,

283
00:19:49,786 --> 00:19:51,147
truly as it was said:

284
00:19:51,319 --> 00:19:56,067
We have inherited the skills of war, generation through generation.

285
00:19:56,568 --> 00:19:58,340
So, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were saying;

286
00:19:58,504 --> 00:20:00,401
We don't want to have a fight with you.

287
00:20:00,964 --> 00:20:03,401
So, what have you done.

288
00:20:03,991 --> 00:20:06,627
Did you really meet with Muhammadﷺ?

289
00:20:08,287 --> 00:20:13,152
The Muslims, among them, among the Al-Aos wal Khazraj(الاوس والخزرج) remained silent,

290
00:20:14,259 --> 00:20:16,275
and the non believers started speaking,

291
00:20:16,315 --> 00:20:17,910
they said; that never happened.

292
00:20:17,990 --> 00:20:21,001
We never met with Muhammadﷺ and they were speaking the truth.

293
00:20:21,317 --> 00:20:24,588
They had no idea of this secret meeting that happened.

294
00:20:25,088 --> 00:20:26,906
Because only the Muslims knew about it

295
00:20:27,176 --> 00:20:30,989
and they kept on refuting that and said we never met with Muhammadﷺ,

296
00:20:31,013 --> 00:20:33,162
we had nothing to do with him, we wouldn't see him.

297
00:20:34,519 --> 00:20:40,060
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: We the Muslims were staring at each other silently and we didn't speak.

298
00:20:42,507 --> 00:20:44,318
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were becoming convinced.

299
00:20:44,365 --> 00:20:48,840
 Now, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said that I wanted to change the topic, I wanted to change the subject.

300
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:55,952
So, there was Al-Haris Bin Hishaam(ألحارث بن هشام), one of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who was present.

301
00:20:57,430 --> 00:21:00,782
He was wearing some new sandals, brand new.

302
00:21:01,290 --> 00:21:02,829
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said;

303
00:21:03,141 --> 00:21:06,504
I told Abu Jabir(ابوجابر), who's one of our seniors

304
00:21:06,845 --> 00:21:08,845
I told him: O Abu Jabir(ابوجابر),

305
00:21:09,250 --> 00:21:14,580
being one of our leaders, you can't even afford to wear new sandals like this young man of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

306
00:21:15,629 --> 00:21:19,009
I mean, what's wrong with you, you're one of our leaders and you wearing this old shoes,

307
00:21:19,239 --> 00:21:22,516
while this young man of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) is wearing these brand new sandals.

308
00:21:23,087 --> 00:21:25,822
Now this young man of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was quite upset by that statement,

309
00:21:25,862 --> 00:21:29,393
I mean, what are you talking about my shoes, so impressed with my shoes.

310
00:21:29,433 --> 00:21:32,861
So, he took them off and threw them to Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

311
00:21:34,235 --> 00:21:35,710
Abu Jabir(ابوجابر) said;

312
00:21:35,972 --> 00:21:41,480
Take it easy Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), you have made the young man angry, give him back his sandals.

313
00:21:42,495 --> 00:21:43,636
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said;

314
00:21:43,803 --> 00:21:45,665
No, I will not give them back to him.

315
00:21:45,747 --> 00:21:50,335
This is a good omen to me, I will take his booty in war.

316
00:21:50,881 --> 00:21:53,900
هَذَا فَعْلٌ حَسَنْ سَاصْلُبُه

317
00:21:54,246 --> 00:21:58,968
This is a good omen, I'm gonna take off from him, spoils of war.

318
00:22:00,958 --> 00:22:02,633
And that was the end of the meeting.

319
00:22:03,554 --> 00:22:07,092
 This meeting between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار),

320
00:22:07,307 --> 00:22:12,806
we can fairly say that it is the most important meeting that Rasool Allah ﷺ had so far.

321
00:22:13,455 --> 00:22:15,343
It was a turning point in Islam.

322
00:22:15,740 --> 00:22:23,714
Finally now, Rasool Allah ﷺ has a solid base to start spreading the message from, with protection,

323
00:22:24,263 --> 00:22:31,460
and freedom to go out and propagate the message of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

324
00:22:32,966 --> 00:22:36,300
This is Baiyah Tul Aqabah As-Thania(بيعة العقبه الثانيه).

325
00:22:36,990 --> 00:22:40,530
Few lessons, and we'll close,

326
00:22:41,529 --> 00:22:51,529
Number one, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), He states that when we left Madina,

327
00:22:51,934 --> 00:22:53,838
 قَدْ صَلَّيْنَا وَ فَقَّهْنَاَ

328
00:22:54,283 --> 00:23:00,726
He said; We have already learned our prayers and understood our religion.

329
00:23:02,235 --> 00:23:05,298
This happened before Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة).

330
00:23:06,599 --> 00:23:11,507
So, for those brothers and sisters who are delaying their learning.

331
00:23:11,817 --> 00:23:16,252
Until somehow they can travel overseas and go and study with the Shuyukh(شيوخ),

332
00:23:16,481 --> 00:23:18,798
or get admission to an Islamic college.

333
00:23:19,132 --> 00:23:21,259
 You're just finding excuses for yourself.

334
00:23:21,610 --> 00:23:23,211
You need to study and learn now.

335
00:23:23,568 --> 00:23:25,859
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: We already learned our prayers

336
00:23:26,133 --> 00:23:29,875
and we understood our religion, even though Rasool Allah ﷺ was not there yet.

337
00:23:30,253 --> 00:23:32,813
It's true that, they had a teacher with them Mus'ab Bin Umair(مصعب بن عمير),

338
00:23:33,065 --> 00:23:38,691
but this statement has a message in it, that we're ready, we're learning.

339
00:23:39,246 --> 00:23:46,012
Don't put off your learnings study Islam, spend time to learn the religion of Allah.

340
00:23:46,322 --> 00:23:48,324
Try to get the best out of the situation.

341
00:23:48,775 --> 00:23:51,319
If you have a Shaikh(شيخ) to teach you, that's the best,

342
00:23:51,549 --> 00:23:55,383
don't have a Shaikh(شيخ), find somebody who's more learned than you,

343
00:23:55,629 --> 00:23:57,717
can't find that, take a book and study.

344
00:23:58,364 --> 00:24:04,970
But don't give it up, don't put it off, because you might never get the time, when you're free to do it.

345
00:24:05,853 --> 00:24:08,413
And procrastination is not an excuse,

346
00:24:08,726 --> 00:24:12,111
on the day of judgment, Ibn Qayyim(ابن قيم) says; when you go through the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an

347
00:24:12,406 --> 00:24:17,444
you'll find that the majority of the screaming of the people of Hellfire in Qur'an,

348
00:24:17,851 --> 00:24:22,147
is because of their procrastination, because they delayed.

349
00:24:22,671 --> 00:24:29,200
They say in Qur'an, the verses the narrate their sayings: O Allah take us back to this world, so that we can believe,

350
00:24:29,529 --> 00:24:31,980
O Allah take us back to this world, so that we can give.

351
00:24:32,178 --> 00:24:34,273
O Allah take us back, it's too late.

352
00:24:34,646 --> 00:24:36,797
 So, don't put it off.

353
00:24:39,763 --> 00:24:40,966
Number two,

354
00:24:42,434 --> 00:24:50,250
When Rasool Allah ﷺ asked the Ansaar(أنصار), his terms of the agreement.

355
00:24:51,322 --> 00:24:54,449
And they said, what will we get back.

356
00:24:55,140 --> 00:24:56,876
What are we getting in an exchange.

357
00:24:57,090 --> 00:24:59,256
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them: Jannah(جنة).

358
00:25:00,211 --> 00:25:05,558
Dear brothers and sisters, in our Islamic work, we should be working for the sake of Jannah(جنة),

359
00:25:05,897 --> 00:25:07,706
to please Allahعَزّوجَلّ .

360
00:25:08,063 --> 00:25:18,175
That should be our objective, not to get fame, not to make money, not for the socializing aspect of it.

361
00:25:18,871 --> 00:25:24,019
We should purify our intentions every time consistently,

362
00:25:24,863 --> 00:25:28,011
and make sure that we're doing everything for the sake of Allah.

363
00:25:28,606 --> 00:25:30,574
This religion needs sacrifice

364
00:25:31,312 --> 00:25:37,194
and if you're waiting for an exchange, if you're waiting for a payback in this world, you might not get it.

365
00:25:38,956 --> 00:25:41,924
 This is a religion that demands you to give it everything.

366
00:25:42,963 --> 00:25:47,962
Because you are getting in an exchange Jannah(جنة), which is more valuable than anything that you could give.

367
00:25:48,786 --> 00:25:50,137
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

368
00:25:50,351 --> 00:25:54,264
What Allah is offering you is very expensive, what Allah is offering you is, Jannah(جنة).

369
00:25:54,896 --> 00:25:56,246
We need to pay the price.

370
00:25:58,202 --> 00:26:08,183
Number three, Rasool Allah ﷺ was very clear in what he's asking others in conveying the message.

371
00:26:08,540 --> 00:26:14,595
Rasool Allah ﷺ made it very clear to the Ansaar(أنصار), that what you are getting into is risky,

372
00:26:16,191 --> 00:26:18,673
what you're getting into is a struggle.

373
00:26:18,943 --> 00:26:23,466
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not promise them wealth, did not promise them power,

374
00:26:23,792 --> 00:26:29,268
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them that you need to protect me, you might be attacked.

375
00:26:30,555 --> 00:26:36,340
So, we need to prepare ourselves as Muslims and realized that this is not an easy walk, it's not a walk in the park.

376
00:26:38,510 --> 00:26:42,764
To establish the religion of Allah, it's a struggle and it demands a lot of sacrifice.

377
00:26:43,350 --> 00:26:45,090
And we need to prepare ourselves for that.

378
00:26:45,170 --> 00:26:46,169
 And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

379
00:26:46,209 --> 00:26:48,943
 اِخْشَوْشَنُوْ فَاِنَّ النِّعْمَ لَا تَدْعُوْنْ

380
00:26:49,381 --> 00:26:53,746
Roughen up, because bounties might not continue forever.

381
00:26:54,596 --> 00:26:56,929
Easy life might not go on for good.

382
00:26:59,171 --> 00:27:02,192
So, we need to be prepared and ready.

383
00:27:04,875 --> 00:27:07,069
Number four,

384
00:27:07,807 --> 00:27:10,707
after the second pledge of Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه)

385
00:27:11,419 --> 00:27:14,235
remember again, Rasool Allah ﷺ met with 70 plus.

386
00:27:14,592 --> 00:27:17,837
And there were some others maybe that were Muslim, who didn't come.

387
00:27:18,457 --> 00:27:26,771
Rasool Allah ﷺ immediately, after taking the pledge of allegiance, asked them to appoint 12 Nuqabaa(نقبآء), twelve leaders.

388
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:32,391
So, he divided them into smaller groups and appointed on them leaders.

389
00:27:32,748 --> 00:27:35,206
So, this shows you that this is an organized religion.

390
00:27:35,488 --> 00:27:41,559
And now since there's a group living away from the organization structure of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

391
00:27:41,911 --> 00:27:46,077
Rasool Ullah wanted them to have their own organizational structure.

392
00:27:46,789 --> 00:27:51,900
So, immediately divided the 70 into groups and appointed 12 leaders among them,

393
00:27:52,083 --> 00:27:58,527
and these are the Nuqabaa(نقبآء), who will report back to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and who, he will give them instructions.

394
00:27:59,953 --> 00:28:06,359
So, this is also another lesson to learn that we need to be organized in a manageable fashion.

395
00:28:07,875 --> 00:28:10,714
Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه said;

396
00:28:11,344 --> 00:28:18,572
إِنِّي أُرِيتُ دَارَ هِجْرَتِكُمْ أريد سبخة ذَاتَ نَخْلٍ بَيْنَ لَابَتَيْنِ وَهُمَا الْحَرَّتَانِ

397
00:28:19,218 --> 00:28:22,360
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I was shown the land of your Hijrah(هجره),

398
00:28:22,808 --> 00:28:29,376
it is a land with a lot of palm trees between two rocky tracks,

399
00:28:30,118 --> 00:28:32,684
Al-Harrah(ألحرة) is a rocky volcanic track.

400
00:28:33,113 --> 00:28:37,765
So, that was the beginning of the Hijrah(هجرة) towards Al-Madina.

401
00:28:38,273 --> 00:28:40,591
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in another Hadith(حديث).

402
00:28:41,536 --> 00:28:44,341
By the way, the Hadith(حديث) that I just mentioned is in Masnad Imam Ahmad (مسند امام احمد).

403
00:28:44,967 --> 00:28:46,770
There's a Hadith(حديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

404
00:28:47,104 --> 00:28:48,228
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

405
00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:52,003
رَأَيْتُ فِي الْمَنَامِ أَنِّي أُهَاجِرُ مِنْ مَكَّةَ إِلَى أَرْضٍ بِهَا نَخْلٌ

406
00:28:52,392 --> 00:28:56,218
فَذَهَبَ وَهَلِي إِلَى أَنَّهَا الْيَمَامَةُ أَوْ هَجَرُ فَإِذَا هِيَ يَثْرِبُ

407
00:28:56,490 --> 00:29:03,571
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, I have seen in my dream that I am migrating from Makkah to a land rich with palm trees.

408
00:29:03,944 --> 00:29:06,960
 I initially thought that it is Yamamah(يمامه) or Hajar(حجر).

409
00:29:07,341 --> 00:29:11,323
But then it turned out to be Yasrib(يثرب), Yasrib(يثرب) is the old name of Madina,

410
00:29:11,749 --> 00:29:14,172
which was changed by Rasool Allah ﷺ

411
00:29:14,513 --> 00:29:18,375
and Rasool Allah ﷺ banned, the use of the name Yasrib(يثرب).

412
00:29:18,682 --> 00:29:23,558
In fact, Rasool Allah ﷺ says if anybody says Yasrib(يثرب), they should make Istaghfar(إستغفار).

413
00:29:24,645 --> 00:29:27,881
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to change the identity of this city,

414
00:29:28,103 --> 00:29:31,222
Yasrib(يثرب) had a history of rivalry and warfare

415
00:29:31,746 --> 00:29:35,826
Rasool Allah ﷺ now is giving it a new identity, it is Madina(مدينه) Madina-Tu-Rasool Allah(مدينةالرسول الله).

416
00:29:36,073 --> 00:29:37,221
What does Madina(مدينه) mean?

417
00:29:37,261 --> 00:29:40,586
It is the town of Rasool Allahﷺ.

418
00:29:41,935 --> 00:29:44,408
Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه), narrates this Hadith(حديث).

419
00:29:45,027 --> 00:29:51,844
She says, we came back from Al-Habashah(الحبشه)

420
00:29:52,730 --> 00:29:58,353
and my husband wanted to go, again to Al-Habashah(الحبشه)

421
00:29:58,393 --> 00:30:04,729
but then he heard that Madina(مدينه) is a new land of Hijrah(هجرة), and that there's some Muslims there.

422
00:30:05,188 --> 00:30:09,301
 So, he decided to take his family and go to Madina.

423
00:30:10,127 --> 00:30:13,308
And that was one year before Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه).

424
00:30:13,745 --> 00:30:17,284
So, he was one of the earliest to go.

425
00:30:19,015 --> 00:30:25,936
So, she said that he mounted me on a camel and he placed my son on my lap

426
00:30:26,878 --> 00:30:29,531
and we were ready to leave Makkah.

427
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:37,446
But my family came to me and said, we're not going to allow you to go with your husband.

428
00:30:37,904 --> 00:30:41,531
We're not going to allow him, to take you with him to that foreign land.

429
00:30:42,867 --> 00:30:45,889
So, they pulled me away, from my husband.

430
00:30:46,881 --> 00:30:52,373
When Bannu Al-Asad(بنو ألأسد) the family of Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) saw that

431
00:30:53,402 --> 00:31:02,241
they came in and said, well we're not going to allow you to take the child, so they took the child with them.

432
00:31:02,858 --> 00:31:05,928
So now, you have Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) is separated from Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه)

433
00:31:05,968 --> 00:31:07,761
and they're both separated from their son.

434
00:31:09,422 --> 00:31:11,627
The family of Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه) took Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه),

435
00:31:12,141 --> 00:31:15,046
the family of Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) took Salamah(سلمه), the child,

436
00:31:15,395 --> 00:31:16,879
and now the three were separated.

437
00:31:17,228 --> 00:31:20,030
So, Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه) ended up making Hijrah(هجرة) alone.

438
00:31:21,044 --> 00:31:25,533
While Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه) and Salamah(سلمه), were separated in Makkah.

439
00:31:27,628 --> 00:31:28,851
Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه) said;

440
00:31:29,484 --> 00:31:39,417
I would go out of my home every day to the valley and sit on a rock and cry, for hours.

441
00:31:39,941 --> 00:31:42,464
And I would do that on a daily basis.

442
00:31:43,195 --> 00:31:45,047
And that continued for about a year.

443
00:31:46,636 --> 00:31:51,363
Imagine this woman, mother missing her husband, missing her child.

444
00:31:51,593 --> 00:31:54,712
She said: I would go out every day in the morning and just cry.

445
00:31:55,744 --> 00:32:02,298
So, then one of Bannu Mugheera(بنومغيرة), my relatives saw the condition I'm in and said to my family.

446
00:32:02,338 --> 00:32:05,274
 This was her uncle, he said to my family, he said,

447
00:32:05,620 --> 00:32:11,207
"Aren't you having any mercy and sympathy on this woman, allow her to go and join her husband."

448
00:32:12,414 --> 00:32:15,718
So, they finally agreed and they told Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه), you are free to leave.

449
00:32:16,709 --> 00:32:21,947
When the family of the husband knew that, they gave her, her son

450
00:32:22,137 --> 00:32:24,193
 and they said now you can join your husband.

451
00:32:24,476 --> 00:32:29,297
So, Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه) picked up her child, Salamah(سلمه) and she went to Madina.

452
00:32:29,337 --> 00:32:31,630
Now she was alone had no one with her.

453
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:37,389
She mounted on a camel with her son and left towards Madina, traveling alone.

454
00:32:39,927 --> 00:32:45,340
When she reached to At-Tanaeem(تنعيم), which is not far away from Makkah, few kilometers outside of Makkah.

455
00:32:45,848 --> 00:32:49,698
She met with Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه),

456
00:32:51,028 --> 00:32:55,448
when he saw her, he said, daughter of Abu Umayyah(ابواميه).

457
00:32:56,416 --> 00:32:57,638
Where are you heading?

458
00:32:58,503 --> 00:33:00,157
She says I'm going to Madina.

459
00:33:00,874 --> 00:33:03,379
He told her, Are you having anybody accompany you?

460
00:33:03,593 --> 00:33:05,069
She said: No, I'm alone.

461
00:33:05,498 --> 00:33:11,699
He said, Well, I would accompany you, it's not appropriate to leave you alone in this travel.

462
00:33:11,945 --> 00:33:14,754
Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه) was a Mushrik(مشرك), he was a non believer.

463
00:33:15,072 --> 00:33:22,688
But he saw this woman, felt sympathy for her and wanted to help her out.

464
00:33:23,857 --> 00:33:29,910
And he was guarding her and protecting her on this journey from between Makkah and Madina.

465
00:33:30,498 --> 00:33:38,950
Ummo Salamahرضي الله عنها , she says, and I swear, I was never in the company of any Arab more honorable than him.

466
00:33:39,874 --> 00:33:43,200
When we made the stop, he would make my camel kneel.

467
00:33:43,708 --> 00:33:47,733
And then he would move away, until I would have dismounted.

468
00:33:48,155 --> 00:33:51,423
And then he would come back and take the camel and tie it.

469
00:33:51,998 --> 00:33:55,611
And then he would leave and go and sleep, under a tree far away from me.

470
00:33:56,151 --> 00:34:00,341
Next day in the morning, he would bring my camel prepare the saddle.

471
00:34:01,510 --> 00:34:05,337
And then he would call me to come and mount and he would leave.

472
00:34:05,662 --> 00:34:08,765
And when I'm on the camel, he would come back,

473
00:34:09,388 --> 00:34:11,768
and then he would guide me through this trip.

474
00:34:12,220 --> 00:34:17,022
And she said, he continued doing that until, we reach to the outskirts of Madina.

475
00:34:18,122 --> 00:34:21,142
And we saw Qubaa(قباء) in the distance, he pointed to Qubaa(قباء) and said,

476
00:34:21,181 --> 00:34:24,404
See that village over there that's where your husband is.

477
00:34:24,737 --> 00:34:26,610
And he said: Now you're on your own.

478
00:34:27,995 --> 00:34:30,707
Ummo Salamah(امّ سلمه), comments and says,

479
00:34:31,243 --> 00:34:35,665
I know of no other family in Islam who suffered like that of Abu Salamah(ابوسلمه).

480
00:34:35,964 --> 00:34:40,876
And I swear I never had a more honorable companion than Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه),

481
00:34:41,056 --> 00:34:47,166
she was impressed, she says that Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه) had so much nobility

482
00:34:47,206 --> 00:34:51,603
because keep in mind the animosity between Muslims and non Muslims.

483
00:34:52,134 --> 00:34:56,917
For so far, Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه) to go out of his way and to accompany a woman who's leaving Makkah

484
00:34:57,012 --> 00:35:00,168
 and that's supposed to be a no-no, you're not supposed to leave Makkah to Madina.

485
00:35:00,586 --> 00:35:05,183
And he went out of his way and supported her and helped her in this honorable fashion.

486
00:35:05,356 --> 00:35:07,363
She liked that, and she appreciated it.

487
00:35:08,223 --> 00:35:10,947
Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه), would later on become Muslim.

488
00:35:11,606 --> 00:35:17,613
After his most of the prominent members of his family were killed in the Battle of Uhud(أحد).

489
00:35:18,164 --> 00:35:22,807
But later on, he did become Muslim, he and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) in the same time.

490
00:35:24,678 --> 00:35:32,900
Also Uthman Bin Talha(عثمان بن طلحه) is from the family, which were the keepers of the keys to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

491
00:35:33,456 --> 00:35:39,872
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ kept the keys with them and the keys are still with them today.

492
00:35:40,492 --> 00:35:48,631
The family of Bannu Abd Ad-Daar(بنو عبد ادار), they are the ones who hold the keys to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), until this day and time.

493
00:35:50,406 --> 00:35:53,027
The next story is the story of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

494
00:35:53,210 --> 00:35:58,429
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه says, when we decided to make Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina.

495
00:35:58,896 --> 00:36:06,865
I agreed with Ayyash Bin Abi Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه) and Hisham Bin Aas(هشام بن العاص) to be company

496
00:36:07,618 --> 00:36:09,452
and to go together to Madina.

497
00:36:09,650 --> 00:36:15,041
 We set an appointed time to meet at Saraf(سرف), this is an area outside of Makkah.

498
00:36:16,763 --> 00:36:24,809
We said, if morning comes and any of us is missing that means the person is detained

499
00:36:25,071 --> 00:36:27,097
 and we should just go ahead and migrate.

500
00:36:28,811 --> 00:36:32,479
Morning came and Hisham Bin Aas(هشام بن العاص) did not show up.

501
00:36:32,519 --> 00:36:36,042
 So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and Ayyash Bin Rabiyah(عياش بن ربيعه) were on their own.

502
00:36:37,667 --> 00:36:41,531
They reached to Madina and this was before the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

503
00:36:41,571 --> 00:36:43,766
Rasool Ullah was the last one to migrate.

504
00:36:44,652 --> 00:36:45,888
They reached to Madina.

505
00:36:46,475 --> 00:36:50,212
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) was the half brother of Ayyash Bin Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه),

506
00:36:50,317 --> 00:36:57,652
so Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) and his brother Al-Haris Bin Hisham(الحارث بن هشام) went all the way to Madina

507
00:36:58,374 --> 00:37:00,903
to bring back Ayyash Bin Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه)

508
00:37:01,626 --> 00:37:06,069
they went to Al-Madina and they told Ayyash(عياش), your mother has made an oath

509
00:37:06,575 --> 00:37:14,152
that she will not comb her hair and she will not take shadow, until you come back.

510
00:37:15,664 --> 00:37:22,327
So, she will remain in the heat under the sun of Makkah and she will not comb her hair, until you come back.

511
00:37:23,679 --> 00:37:24,891
The exact statement was,

512
00:37:24,923 --> 00:37:30,094
"your mother has warned that she will not allow, a comb to touch her hair, until she sees you,

513
00:37:30,264 --> 00:37:32,500
nor will she shelter from the sun.

514
00:37:34,380 --> 00:37:36,024
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was listening.

515
00:37:36,397 --> 00:37:39,032
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told Ayyash Bin Abi Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه)

516
00:37:40,086 --> 00:37:42,015
these people want to deceive you.

517
00:37:42,316 --> 00:37:45,221
They want to entice you and take you back, it's a trick.

518
00:37:46,484 --> 00:37:52,474
And regarding the oath of your mother, when her hair is filled with lice, she will comb

519
00:37:52,907 --> 00:37:56,092
and when she feels a severe heat of Makkah she will take shelter.

520
00:37:56,689 --> 00:37:58,639
So, forget about it and don't go with them.

521
00:37:59,599 --> 00:38:01,544
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he says;

522
00:38:01,584 --> 00:38:03,488
 لَسْتُ بِلْ خِبْ وَالْخِبِّ يَخْدَاعْنِيْ

523
00:38:04,381 --> 00:38:07,065
I'm not a man who tricks others.

524
00:38:07,938 --> 00:38:10,485
Neither do, I allow anybody to trick me.

525
00:38:12,099 --> 00:38:13,985
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told Ayyash Bin Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه)

526
00:38:14,033 --> 00:38:14,993
don't go with them.

527
00:38:15,033 --> 00:38:18,050
Ayyash Bin Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه) he was now feeling sorry for his mother

528
00:38:18,090 --> 00:38:20,593
 and Umar(عُمَر) wasn't able to convince him.

529
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:23,904
Ayyash Bin Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه) decided that he's gonna go with them.

530
00:38:25,863 --> 00:38:31,290
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), told him well, if you insist, then at least take this camel of mine with you.

531
00:38:32,465 --> 00:38:34,758
This is a fast and strong camel.

532
00:38:35,306 --> 00:38:40,798
If you ever feel suspicious, run away.

533
00:38:43,380 --> 00:38:50,096
So, Ayyash Bin Rabiyah(عياش بن ربيعه), Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) and Al-Haris Bin Hisham(الحارث بن هشام) are now on their way back to Makkah.

534
00:38:50,326 --> 00:38:53,007
 Everyone has their own camel.

535
00:38:53,507 --> 00:38:55,968
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) started complaining about his camel.

536
00:38:56,566 --> 00:38:59,809
What a horrible camel, it's too difficult, slow.

537
00:39:00,918 --> 00:39:03,188
And then he told Ayyash Bin Abi Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه).

538
00:39:03,474 --> 00:39:05,931
Can you please switch camels just for a while.

539
00:39:05,971 --> 00:39:08,085
I mean, this camel of mine is causing me trouble.

540
00:39:09,101 --> 00:39:12,029
Ayyash Bin Abi Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه), beings a nice man, he is, agreed.

541
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:18,612
So, they now stopped the camels and they had the camels kneel down.

542
00:39:20,187 --> 00:39:27,310
As soon as the camel of Ayyash(عياش) reached the ground, both men attacked him and tied him up.

543
00:39:28,496 --> 00:39:31,979
And they dragged him into Makkah and they enticed him and he apostated.

544
00:39:33,527 --> 00:39:36,914
And the same thing has happened to Hisham Ibn Al-Aas(هشام إبن ألعآص),

545
00:39:36,990 --> 00:39:39,596
 the third partner who was detained in Makkah.

546
00:39:40,738 --> 00:39:42,239
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

547
00:39:43,295 --> 00:39:48,071
We used to say among ourselves, the Muslims, that whoever stayed behind

548
00:39:48,642 --> 00:39:55,384
and foot in and was enticed by the non believers, Allahسبحانه وتعالى will never forgive them.

549
00:39:56,879 --> 00:39:58,513
That was the understanding we had.

550
00:39:58,839 --> 00:40:05,447
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said and that was also the understanding going around among, the ones who stay behind.

551
00:40:05,724 --> 00:40:07,790
They felt that they have lost hope, that's it.

552
00:40:08,431 --> 00:40:13,056
You have apostated, there is no way Allah can forgive your sins.

553
00:40:13,683 --> 00:40:16,318
And that was their common understanding for a while.

554
00:40:16,628 --> 00:40:22,199
Until Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina and received the revelation.

555
00:40:22,619 --> 00:40:24,143
 Allahسبحانه وتعالى says;

556
00:40:24,838 --> 00:40:35,630
قُلْ يَا عِبَادِيَ الَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُوا عَلَىٰ أَنْفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوا مِنْ رَحْمَةِ اللَّهِ

557
00:40:36,940 --> 00:40:42,010
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا ۚ

558
00:40:42,267 --> 00:40:47,949
إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ۝

559
00:40:48,286 --> 00:41:02,886
وَأَنِيبُوا إِلَىٰ رَبِّكُمْ وَأَسْلِمُوا لَهُ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ ثُمَّ لَا تُنْصَرُونَ۝

560
00:41:03,536 --> 00:41:17,208
وَاتَّبِعُوا أَحْسَنَ مَا أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ

561
00:41:17,790 --> 00:41:29,193
مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ بَغْتَةً وَأَنْتُمْ لَا تَشْعُرُونَ۝

562
00:41:30,123 --> 00:41:36,451
Say, O My servants who have harmed themselves, do not despair of God's mercy.

563
00:41:37,597 --> 00:41:39,306
Allah will forgive all sins.

564
00:41:39,640 --> 00:41:42,140
 He is the all forgiving, the All Merciful.

565
00:41:42,621 --> 00:41:46,499
Turn back to your Lord and submit to Him before punishment reaches you.

566
00:41:47,042 --> 00:41:48,688
Then you shall not be helped,

567
00:41:49,426 --> 00:41:55,361
follow the best that has been revealed to you from your Lord, before punishment comes suddenly to you.

568
00:41:55,668 --> 00:41:57,494
And you are caught unaware.

569
00:41:59,630 --> 00:42:06,009
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wrote this verse and he sent it to Hisham Ibn Al-Aas(هشام إبن ألعآص),

570
00:42:06,996 --> 00:42:09,266
Hisham Ibn Al-Aas(هشام إبن ألعآص) was the one, who was detained in Makkah.

571
00:42:09,813 --> 00:42:14,943
Hisham Ibn Al-Aas(هشام إبن ألعآص) said: I received that verse, and I would go up to Tuwaa(طوى)

572
00:42:16,406 --> 00:42:21,221
and I would read it, and reread it and I would read it again and again and again,

573
00:42:21,261 --> 00:42:27,215
for a few days I would go out in this area and just keep on reading that verse

574
00:42:27,255 --> 00:42:32,312
trying to understand, why Umar(عُمَر) sent it to me? What is the meaning of this verse.?

575
00:42:32,595 --> 00:42:36,529
Until I understood that this verse was revealed talking about us

576
00:42:37,746 --> 00:42:42,061
and say that no matter, what you do Allah can still forgive you.

577
00:42:42,298 --> 00:42:45,518
If you seek forgiveness, no matter what happened.

578
00:42:45,954 --> 00:42:53,123
Even if you stayed behind, even if you were enticed by the non believers, you still have a chance you shouldn't give up.

579
00:42:55,191 --> 00:42:57,088
Hisham Ibn Al-Aas(هشام إبن ألعآص) said;

580
00:42:57,398 --> 00:43:02,052
I asked Allah for forgiveness, mounted my camel and went towards Al-Madina.

581
00:43:04,463 --> 00:43:05,765
Two lessons to learn from this.

582
00:43:05,805 --> 00:43:06,695
Number one,

583
00:43:07,019 --> 00:43:08,081
 the forgiveness of Allah,

584
00:43:08,253 --> 00:43:11,937
Allah is all forgiving, no matter what you do, never give up.

585
00:43:12,136 --> 00:43:13,628
Ask Allah to forgive you.

586
00:43:14,795 --> 00:43:21,432
The greatest sin which is Shirk(شرك) if a person repents from it, and goes back to Allah, Allah will forgive it.

587
00:43:24,076 --> 00:43:28,383
But one needs to ask Allah for forgiveness before the punishment comes because Allah سبحانه وتعالى says,

588
00:43:28,834 --> 00:43:32,016
turn back to your Lord and submit to Him before punishment reaches you.

589
00:43:32,491 --> 00:43:34,347
You need to do it before, it's too late.

590
00:43:35,029 --> 00:43:36,410
Second lesson,

591
00:43:37,601 --> 00:43:44,394
Beware of the non believers beware, be careful.

592
00:43:45,132 --> 00:43:48,193
Ayyash Bin Abi Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه) trusted Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

593
00:43:48,733 --> 00:43:50,621
How can you trust such a person?

594
00:43:51,510 --> 00:43:58,033
Don't let the sweet words and the nice talk of the enemies of Allah sway you.

595
00:44:00,053 --> 00:44:01,430
Some of us are naive.

596
00:44:01,541 --> 00:44:06,311
They hear a good comment here and there, they're nice statement that is coming from this politician or that

597
00:44:06,700 --> 00:44:07,966
and they fall in the trap.

598
00:44:08,713 --> 00:44:15,293
Beware somebody who has a long record of fighting Islam, their record should speak for them,

599
00:44:17,269 --> 00:44:18,880
so we shouldn't be tricked.

600
00:44:20,342 --> 00:44:25,974
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), this plot of Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) did not pass on him, he knew

601
00:44:26,442 --> 00:44:29,280
and he told Ayyash Bin Abi Rabiyah(عياش بن أبي ربيعه), don't believe them.

602
00:44:29,518 --> 00:44:30,558
They're lying

603
00:44:31,200 --> 00:44:35,361
and your mother her head gets filled with lice, she will have to comb it.

604
00:44:36,211 --> 00:44:38,600
And no one will survive in the heat of Makkah.

605
00:44:39,049 --> 00:44:41,158
That's an oath that she will have to break.

606
00:44:41,555 --> 00:44:42,896
So, we should be careful.

607
00:44:43,673 --> 00:44:44,936
And Allahسبحانه وتعالى says;

608
00:44:44,976 --> 00:44:46,136
 وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِأَعْدَائِكُمْ

609
00:44:46,176 --> 00:44:46,974
Allah knows your enemies.

610
00:44:47,052 --> 00:44:49,669
And he has told us who our enemies are, we shouldn't fall in the trap,

611
00:44:49,803 --> 00:44:52,175
We should be careful and we should beware.

